        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(flows): swallow heartbeat write rejections from setInterval",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFlow node heartbeats schedule `void heartbeat()` on a `setInterval`. If\n`store.writeLive` rejects (disk full, removed run dir, teardown race),\nthat becomes an unhandledRejection from the timer callback.\n\n## Evidence\n\nFocused regression that forces writeLive to reject and asserts zero\nunhandledRejection while the timer keeps firing:\n\n```console\n$ tsx --test test/flows-heartbeat-rejection.test.ts\n✔ heartbeat timer boundary swallows writeLive rejections\nℹ tests 1\nℹ pass 1\nℹ fail 0\n```\n\nProduction boundary (unchanged intent):\n\n```ts\nvoid heartbeat().catch(() => {\n  // ignore\n});\n```\n\n## Summary\n\n- Catch rejected heartbeat writes at the timer boundary (best-effort)\n- Regression test documents the unhandledRejection contract\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n- **Behavior or issue addressed:** rejected heartbeat writeLive no longer emits unhandledRejection\n- **Real environment tested:** macOS, Node 22+, branch fix/flow-heartbeat-rejection\n- **Exact steps or command run after this patch:** `tsx --test test/flows-heartbeat-rejection.test.ts`\n- **Evidence after fix:** terminal output above (pass; no unhandledRejection with forced disk-full write)\n- **Observed result after fix:** multiple heartbeat attempts with rejections produce zero unhandledRejection events\n- **What was not tested:** multi-node live flow against a real agent with injected FS failures\n\n## Related\n\n- ClawSweeper: live/regression proof for rejected timer write\n- Same file already uses `.catch(() => {})` for onTimeout cancellation\n",
